  "body": " Finite-variable presentation   Every rational localisation of is bicontinuously isomorphic to a ring of the form where is a rational localisation of one of the strongly noetherian Tate rings .   Lean (finite-variable model)  Lean (existence of the model)   Start with a rational datum in . Choose a scalar with and small enough that lie in . Multiplying the datum by does not change the rational subset or its localisation, so we may assume that lie in . Choose a neighbourhood as in . By , for some there are such that By , the datum gives the same rational subset and the same completed localisation. It is rational in , so applying to a Bezout identity for its entries shows that it is already a rational datum in . Now apply .   "
