  "number": "8.9",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  The ring is an integral domain but is not uniform.   Lean (chart is a domain)  Lean (chart is nonuniform)   Put . Here denotes the ring of all coefficient families indexed by finite-support multi-indices. Multiplication is convolution. For a fixed there are only finitely many decompositions , so every coefficient of a product is a finite sum. Order by comparing two vectors at the largest index where they differ. This is an additive well-order. If two series are nonzero, the coefficient at the sum of their least nonzero exponents is the product of the corresponding coefficients and is nonzero. Thus is a domain.  The coefficient description gives a homomorphism It is a homomorphism by . If its image is zero, then for every . Since is a domain, every is zero. The map is therefore injective, and hence is a domain.  Inside write and put Formula gives The even powers of have norm at most , and the odd powers have norm at most . Thus every is power-bounded. The family is not bounded, since its norms are unbounded. Hence is unbounded and is not uniform.   "
